 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n\nActivity                                                                                        Path:\n\nEnter Period Consumption for Interval Meters                    Move-in process or manual maintenance by choosing |}*SAP Easy Access >\nSAP menu > Utilities Industry \u00bb Device Management > Device Installation >\nInstallation Structure > Period Consumption J\n\nDefine Minimum Share for Interval Meters (Optional)          |/SAP Implementation Guide > SAP Utilities > Contract Billing > Billing\nMaster Data > Rate Structure > Rates > Define Rates J\n\nFor use during mass simulation: Define simulation               |PSAP Easy Access > SAP menu > Utilities Industry > Billing > Mass\nperiods, information structure version numbers and any | Simulation > Settings / Preparation >|\nsimulation indexes\n\nFeatures\n\nSimulation is performed according to the following rules that apply to all profile time slices that are assigned to a time-of-use rate\nin the simulation period:\n\nMeasured Profile Values\n\n\"0\" Values in Lock Period\n\nCopy Profile Values Measured\nin the Past\n\nsynthetic Profile Adjusted to\nAnnual Consumption Measured\n\nsynthetic Profile Adjusted to\nPeriod Consumption for the Interval Meter\n\nTime-of-Use Simulation Rules\n\nTo simulate rate steps, access billing in the simulation mode or perform periodic billing with integrated budget billing simulation.\n\nYou access the transaction for individual billing simulation in the SAP menu under !\u00aeUtilities Industrv \u00ae Billing \u00ae Billing\n",
